# Scenario 1 of docs/reverse-engineering/verification-protocol.md: straight line.
#
# Full thrust, no steering, for 200 ticks. Isolates acceleration and drag: the
# only forces acting are the engine, the passive resistances and whatever the
# hover probes find under the ship.
#
# This is deliberately identical to the `--hold cross` capture that
# docs/reverse-engineering/ppsspp-debugger.md#the-reference-scenario already
# documents as working. It exists so the scripted path can be checked against a
# result that was measured before scripts existed: a capture taken with
# `--script straight-line.inputs` and one taken with `--hold cross` must agree,
# and if they do not, the script machinery is what changed, not the physics.
#
# Reference scenario: Time Trial, Venom, Talon's Junction White
# (Data\Environments\16_Track), Assegai. Start the capture with `--warmup`
# large enough to be past the countdown - holding thrust through it is a false
# start, which is why a script's warmup holds nothing.

200 cross
